 ## Troubleshooting
+
+For J2 capture ownership on `fix/followup-capture`, inspect the additive
+`capture_ownership` block in the stopped run's `run_summary.json`. It records
+whether the scene and target were known at start, display updates, rejection
+reasons, accepted ambiguity, dropped/unpaired work and stale generations.
+NotGameView has separate show-flag, game-thread-view and controller-ID counts.
+These are request/family checks, not frame counts. Mask-served includes census
+and probe requests. Labels do not carry these diagnostics.
+
+Checkpoint I stays on its host. Run
+`python tools/office_checkpoint_i.py SESSION --host 1 --case 11 --inspection inspections.json`
+from a checkout with the reader's dependencies installed. Host 1 is the first
+office host; host 2 is the second. The inspection file must contain at least
+20 distributed, independently inspected PNG hashes; ownership counters cannot
+substitute for looking at the pictures. Cases 11–14, whole-session input,
+the check digit and failure-counter ordering are documented in
+[`tools/office_checkpoint_i.md`](../tools/office_checkpoint_i.md).
+Type only the resulting short case lines into chat; captures, logs and client
+files stay on the host. Home tests do not qualify an office host.
+
 - **"The following modules are missing or built with a different engine version… rebuild?"** —
   expected if `Binaries/` is stale or absent. Click **Yes**, or run step 4 first.
